  "implementation": [
    "Two additive APIs return existing reconciliation input and compact correction predecessor types after validating a full supplied retained archive. Existing record shapes and public entrypoints remain unchanged.",
    "Retained recovery binds the selected original submission to its confirmed ordered journal, exact saved XML/document keys and canonical requested confirmation IDs. Saved confirmation JSON layout is preserved; a later correction does not erase confirmed ancestor recovery.",
    "Retained correction validates full captured source/approval/claim relations and the entire unfiltered company/year filing chain. It selects the exact accepted/rejected terminal leaf, validates original actor, manifest, feedback originals and reconciliation set, and requires confirmed full-year dispatch.",
    "The existing capture guard applies to any v2 source or v3 approval anywhere in typed input. Legacy-only unknown capture stays unknown. Genuine no-activity parents remain supported; a managed full-year head cannot be hidden by filtering.",
    "Three private fixed-callback extractions share mechanics with old APIs while retaining their original validators and error order. No application, adapter, HTTP, SQL, writer or provider caller switches in this slice."
  ],
